# macOS/iCloud duplicate artefacts. This machine produces "name 2.ext" copies during
# sync, and a blanket `git add -A` will happily commit them — 20 of them reached the
# repo once, including a second copy of the 2.8MB WordPress export and stale duplicates
# of every lib/*.ts that then drift from the originals.
